From: MiaAI_Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 09:00:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] glm cuda: E4M3 latent caches on KV pages, and KV sharding
 (TF_GLM_KV_SHARD)

The 2x RTX PRO 6000 recipe's GLM stack, ported from TensorFold 1.3.0 (81de26f6) to 1.3.5 onto main's latent
Shape (rows of kv_lora + qk_rope, the pool a parameter), its roped 576-wide path and its index geometry:

- E4M3 (--kv-cache fp8) latent rows on KV pages: each cache's part of a page holds its codes, then their fp32
  scales, then the pooled keys (Shape.format); the paged _fp8 chunk and latent-write kernels; the snapshot plan
  copies codes and scales as their own parts. TF_KV_PAGES on/1/all (and any other text, as before) pages E4M3
  too; auto keeps whole windows for E4M3.
- An E4M3 cache's sparse token lists stay positions (Table.logical): its chunks take each key through the table.
- A reply the pool cannot hold opens with the longest reply the pool holds for its prompt.
- KV sharding at TP=2 (TF_GLM_KV_SHARD=1): each stream's E4M3 latent rows on its owner GPU, owner-computed
  decode and verify, prompts on a borrowed twin, kept states carried between owners; latent rows are always
  written and read through the latent table (the target MTP head's prompt rows included). New here: refused by
  name beside --learn-conversations, whose GLM disk images (new in 1.3.x) hold whole states.
- Tests: the stack's host tests on main's APIs, tf-cuda-test glm-kv-shard-check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
